{
  "about": "Experiment E's arms and cells for send-admission-e.toml (docs/journal/2026-11-send-admission-e.md). An experiment is one cell's parameters with one arm's, plus bins_artifact and rep. The cells are Experiment D's rule cells, W4 at 256 KiB and U, without the W4 cells at k = 4 and 56, which every D arm that sent pieces passed; each W4 cell runs on hv03, where D ran W4 at 1 MiB. The TLS arms use a 16,448-byte slot, which holds one whole TLS record. The plaintext arms repeat D's O0 whole and O0 gated 128 KiB on this build. budget is O7w, R = 32, the runtime's default order. tls-O0-gated-85k (a third of a 256 KiB send buffer) runs only in W4-k128-256k, W2-s6 and W4-k128 (journal, Addendum). plain-O0-gated-64k, plain-O0-gated-32k and tls-O0-gated-32k run in every cell (journal, Addendum 2). The 16k arms and the s64k arms (128 slots of 64 KiB, 8 MiB as 512 x 16 KiB is) run in every cell (journal, Addendum 3). Addendum 4 (journal) runs in W2-s6 and W2-s6-p4 only, four runs each: the s64k-512 arms (512 slots of 64 KiB) and s16k-128 arms (128 slots of 16 KiB); and plain-O0-gated-128k-s64k, two more runs in W2-s6 as a control and four in W2-s6-p4, W2 with pipeline 4. W2-s6-p4 runs no other arm; every cell above means every cell but W2-s6-p4.",
